diff --git a/docs/android.md b/docs/android.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a721de7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/android.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# Android embedding research port
+
+The Android target selects Vulkan (`--no-default-features --features vulkan`). It
+reuses Linux POSIX clocks, threads, file-backed VM views and IOSurface stand-ins;
+its own window module explicitly closes a library-owned window request. Embed
+through display callbacks and frame targets. No SDL or AppKit is linked.
+
+`REIMS_VGPU_FRAME_READBACK=buffer` selects a reused shared buffer for embedding frame
+targets. Each frame appends its whole-image copy to its own draw command buffer, so
+the normal frame wait covers the copy; reading pixels copies completed coherent buffer
+bytes and preserves row padding. It adds one target-sized allocation per frame target.
+The default reads the texture as before. No guest texture's CPU-copy behavior changes.
+
+Set `REIMS_VGPU_SHADER_CACHE_DIR` to an absolute app-private directory before the
+first library call. Android app processes generally have no `HOME`; the explicit
+directory takes precedence over the desktop default. Android's shader records
+are bounded to 1 GiB. No guest shaders are bundled by this port.
+
+The current aarch64 raw accesses contain LSE and RCpc instructions and rely on
+LSE2 for unaligned atomics. This research build uses `-C target-feature=+lse,+rcpc`.
+The embedding host must check `AT_HWCAP` for atomics, lrcpc and uscat before loading
+it. It is not a generic ARM64 Android build.
+
+Observed 2026-11-14: cross-target cargo check and a shared-library link passed on
+an arm64 Mac with Rust1.98.1 and Android NDK30. An initial C API run on one Lenovo
+TB373FU stopped at the missing shader cache directory; the explicit directory
+option addresses that observed initialization failure. Guest GPU commands and
+macOS desktop rendering remain untested. Desktop Mac/Linux regression suites
+have not been run for this research patch; it is not claimed merge-ready.
+
+Memory remains a separate integration task. Linux's imports of memfd layouts
+need `VK_EXT_external_memory_host` or `/dev/udmabuf`. This tablet lists no former
+extension and has no latter node. A separate authored Android HardwareBuffer
+probe imported 64 KiB into raw Vulkan and read16384 GPU-filled words through a
+CPU lock, but this does not implement arbitrary aliases of guest pages. No
+copy degradation or guest-visible semantic guard is disabled here.
+
+For an explicitly selected offscreen loader, set `REIMS_VGPU_VULKAN_LOADER` to its
+absolute shared-library path before the first call. Leaving it unset keeps the
+platform's own Vulkan loader. This permits testing a CPU ICD independently of
+the hardware driver; it does not imply hardware acceleration.
+
+Observed on the first Henge guest boot: the arm64 mapper's descriptor-table write
+attempted a 4 KiB view, failing core's `memory.map.mapping_length_unaligned` guard
+before any GPU register writes. Android's mapper now uses the existing guest
+`APV_PAGE_SIZE`/`APV_PAGE_SHIFT` for descriptor counts, table views and guest page
+numbers. The POSIX VM retains the real host kernel page size. The mapping guard
+is unchanged; Mac/Linux mapper behavior is unchanged. This separation needs a
+fresh real-guest run; it is not a completed-desktop claim.
+
+The follow-up guest run passed mapper initialization and negotiated protocol209,
+then refused surface creation. The same distinction also applies to
+`surface_spec`'s client ranges: one host address per guest page must carry16KiB,
+not4KiB. Android now uses the mapper's guest page size for those range lengths as
+well; the Linux surface backend retains its host-page checks and exact aliases.
+
+Android device admission requires VK_EXT_external_memory_host before adopting the
+GPU. The guest and GPU share actual RAM pages; a SwiftShader device without this
+extension is reported unavailable instead of aborting later in EFI MMIO. Runtime
+preference order is preserved among usable devices. This is a prerequisite, not
+a guarantee that every import or shader will succeed.
